e, but we would have no singles to improve except drawing new tiles to make pairs. Passing keeps T2 and T3, which are near each other and could become a Chow or pairs. Also, by not Chi-ing, we avoid giving information to others. The previous player discarded T1, which might be safe for them. Since we are not in a strong position, it's better to keep options and not expose melds prematurely.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
