Chicken Hand\" (8 fan) - defined as hand worth 0 fan otherwise, but with flower tiles not included. Actually Chicken Hand is worth 8 fan if the hand would otherwise be 0 fan. But I already have at least 1 fan from W9 Pung, so not Chicken.\n\nThus, I might be unable to reach 8 fan with current hand unless I get lucky with a high fan pattern from the final tile, like Last Tile Draw (8 fan) or Robbing Kong (8 fan), etc. But those depend on game state.\n\nLooking at game history: many tiles have been played. The wall is likely low. Last Tile Draw might be possible if I draw the last tile. Also, \"Last Tile\" (4 fan) if the winning tile is the last of its kind (three others exposed). Could check tile counts: For example, W9: I have a pung, so all four W9 are out (my pung is three, and one more? unshown shows 0 left, so all four accounted for). So if I win with a tile that has three others exposed, I get 4 fan. For instance, if I win with T8: unshown T8 left 2, but in history many T8 played? History: Previous played T8, I have T8 in hand, next played T8? Actually next player history: Play T8. So T8 has been played at least once. Not sure if three are exposed.\n\nGiven the complexity, perhaps the safest is to discard the least useful tile to improve chances of drawing a winning tile that also gives fan. F2 is an honor, discarding it might reduce fan potential but also remove a tile that could form a pung for Seat Wind. However, keeping F2 and hoping for F2 pung gives 2+1=3 fan from that pung, plus W9 pung 1 = 4, plus maybe other patterns. Still not 8.\n\nMaybe I need to change strategy: aim to win with a pair of F2 and a meld from W3/W6/T8, and rely on additional fan from waiting patterns or last tile. For example, if I win by Self Drawn (1) + Last Tile (4) + Pung of Terminals (1) + maybe No Honors (1) if no honors = 7, still not 8. Need one more like Single Wait (1) if single wait. Single Wait: winning tile completes a pair. If I have a pair waiting, that's 1 fan. So if I